### 1.3 Migrate Unit Columns from Free-Text to FK References

#### [MODIFY] [schema.ts](file:///d:/dev/acme/acme-erp/server/db/schema.ts)

**Problem**: Currently `items.unit`, `items.purchaseUnit`, `items.saleUnit`, `poItems.unit`, `grnItems.unit`, and `itemUnitPrices.unit` store unit names/symbols as free-text strings (e.g., `"box"`, `"pcs"`). This prevents reliable unit conversion lookups and creates data integrity issues (typos, inconsistent casing).

1. **Add new FK columns**:
   - `items`: `baseUnitId: integer("base_unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`, `purchaseUnitId: integer("purchase_unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`, `saleUnitId: integer("sale_unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`
   - `poItems`: `unitId: integer("unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`
   - `grnItems`: `unitId: integer("unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`
   - `itemUnitPrices`: `unitId: integer("unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)`

2. **Data migration script**: Write a migration script that matches existing text values against `unitTypes.symbol` and `unitTypes.name` (case-insensitive) to populate the new FK columns. If any unmatched text unit is found, auto-create a new `unitTypes` record with category `'Count/Quantity'`.

3. **Drop legacy text columns**: Once the migration script verifies all records have valid FK IDs, drop the old text columns (`items.unit`, `items.purchase_unit`, `items.sale_unit`, `po_items.unit`, `grn_items.unit`, `item_unit_prices.unit`).

4. **All new inventory tables** (`stock_requisition_items`, `stock_transfer_items`, `sales_invoice_items`, `purchase_invoice_items`) use `unitId: integer("unit_id").notNull().references(() => unitTypes.id)` from day one — zero free-text unit columns.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The database schema and models are updated cleanly to use `unitId` / `purchaseUnitId` / `saleUnitId` FKs. Legacy text unit columns will be completely removed during the migration.

