### 1.7 Integrate GRN Posting with Stock Engine

#### [MODIFY] [purchases.ts](file:///d:/dev/acme/acme-erp/server/routes/purchases.ts)

Modify all three GRN save endpoints (`.post("/purchase-orders/:id/grns")`, `.patch("/purchase-orders/:id/grns/:grnId")`, `.post("/grns")`, `.patch("/grns/:grnId")`) to detect when `status` transitions to `'posted'`:

**On GRN Post (`status === 'posted'`)**:
1. Require `storeId` on the GRN (return 400 if missing).
2. For each `grnItem` where `receivedQty > 0`:
   a. Call `findOrCreateBatch(tx, { itemId, batchNumber: item.batch, expiryDate: item.expiryDate, mrp: item.salePrice, purchaseRate: item.unitRate, saleRate: item.salePrice, supplierId: grn.vendorId })`.
   b. Write `batchId` back to the `grnItems` row.
   c. Call `recordStockMovement(tx, { storeId, itemId, batchId, movementType: 'GRN', referenceType: 'GRN', referenceId: grn.id, quantityChange: item.receivedQty + item.freeQty, costPrice: item.unitRate, salePrice: item.salePrice, userId })`.
3. **Lock posted GRNs**: Add guard at start of PATCH/DELETE handlers — if existing GRN status is `'posted'`, return `400 "Posted GRNs cannot be modified. Use a stock adjustment or purchase return."`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Existing `draft` GRN behavior remains **completely unchanged**. The stock engine only activates on the `draft → posted` transition.

