#### Backend Endpoints (in `server/routes/inventory.ts`)

Purchase invoice routes are integrated directly into the `inventory.ts` router under `/inventory/purchase-invoices`:

- `POST /inventory/purchase-invoices` — Create draft invoice (link to vendor, GRN, PO; add line items)
- `GET /inventory/purchase-invoices` — List with filters (`?vendorId=&status=&dateFrom=&dateTo=&page=&pageSize=`)
- `GET /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id` — Detail with items and payment history
- `PATCH /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id` — Update draft invoice
- `PATCH /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id/verify` — Mark as verified (3-way match: PO qty vs GRN qty vs invoice qty)
- `PATCH /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id/approve` — Approve for payment
- `POST /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id/payments` — Record payment against invoice
- `DELETE /inventory/purchase-invoices/:id` — Delete (only if `draft`)
- `GET /inventory/purchase-invoices/pending` — List invoices due/overdue for payment

**3-Way Matching Logic** (on verify):
1. For each invoice line item, compare `invoiceQty` against `grnItem.receivedQty` and `poItem.orderedQty`.
2. Flag mismatches (over-billed, under-billed) but allow verification with remarks.
3. Auto-populate invoice items from GRN items when creating from a GRN.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Decoupled from Accounts Module**: Purchase Invoices and invoice payments remain contained strictly within the Inventory/Purchasing workflow (for 3-way matching, vendor liability tracking, and purchase auditing). They do **NOT** generate entries in `bankExpenses`, `expenditures`, or daily financial closing reports.

